# The data of a launch is not completed (the book, call-receivers; only fn, sub and catch complete their data, when the
# graph is built): Body declares y, the data given has no such place -- answer 3 -- and nothing of the body ran.
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds the call main().
fn: tick () int (int: calls 0)
    calls := calls + 1
    return: calls
sub: main () (
    Args:
        int: a 5
    Other:
        int: x 10
    Body:
        x := tick()
        int: y
        y := x + a
        return: y
    int: response 0
)
    response := fncall(Args Other int Body)
main()
